.TH AVR\-JOB\-LIST 1 "" "avr 0.1.5" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-job-list \- List jobs for an organization.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr job list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List jobs for an organization.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr job list
    avr job list --status failure --limit 5
    avr job list --status in_progress --json job_name,state,conclusion
    avr job list --since 24h
    avr job list --json '?'           # list available fields
    avr job list --json '*'           # all fields
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    completed_at, conclusion, created_at, duration_seconds, platform_job_id,
    platform_run_id, job_id, job_name, labels, repository, repository_id,
    running_on_avrea, started_at, state
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter by repository (org/repo or rep-xxx, repeatable). Auto-detected from git remote if omitted. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter by job name (repeatable). (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Filter by state (queued, in_progress, completed) or conclusion (success, failure, ...). Repeatable. (choices: action_required, cancelled, completed, failure, in_progress, neutral, queued, skipped, stale, startup_failure, success, timed_out; repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-avrea\fR / \fB\-\-shadowing\fR
Filter by Avrea-run vs shadowing jobs.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workflow\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter by workflow ID (wfl-xxx, repeatable). (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fITEXT\fR
Relative time window: '7d', '24h', etc.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max jobs to return. (default: 20)
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fITEXT\fR
Pagination cursor from a previous response.
.TP
\fB\-\-order\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Sort order. (choices: created_at.desc, created_at.asc; default: created_at.desc)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-job (1),
.BR avr-job-logs (1),
.BR avr-job-metrics (1),
